walee"],"released":"May 21, 2026","meta":null,"langs":["English","French","German","Spanish - Spain","Simplified Chinese","Japanese","Korean","Portuguese - Brazil","Russian","Traditional Chinese","Polish"],"min":[["OS","Windows 11 64-bit"],["Processor","Intel Core i5-8600K / AMD Ryzen 5 2600"],["Memory","8 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Nvidia GeForce GTX 1060 6GB / AMD Radeon RX 580"],["DirectX","Version 12"],["Storage","15 GB available space"]],"rec":[["OS","Windows 11 64-bit"],["Processor","Intel Core i5-10600K / AMD Ryzen 5 3600"],["Memory","8 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Nvidia GeForce GTX 1660 / AMD Radeon RX 590"],["DirectX","Version 12"],["Storage","15 GB available space"]],"deck":3,"blurb":"Luna Abyss is a story-driven action-adventure from Kwalee Labs. You play Fawkes, a prisoner sent to a vast structure on the Moon called Luna. Bound by a prophecy that no one fully explains, Fawkes must travel through the depths of this place while serving a sentence. The game combines exploration with platforming and gunfights against enemies that fill the screen with projectiles.\n\nIt is a single-player game, so expect a focused campaign with a dark science-fiction tone. Combat leans toward dodging dense patterns of bullets, which calls for good reflexes. Luna Abyss suits players who like shooters with a strong atmosphere and movement-heavy combat, and who enjoy a story that leaves a few questions open."}}